13 0 obj
<<
/Title (Mashal: Imagine, Rabosai, a wealthy gevir who marries off his daughter to a top bachur from Lakewood. For the chasunah, the shvigger decides she must buy the young couple the most magnificent piece of silver for their kredenz to show off. She goes to an overpriced silversmith in Boro Park and commissions a solid silver becher. The silversmith pours a massive block of sterling silver, carves the outside with incredibly intricate designs of the Shivvas HaMinim, and polishes it until it is blinding. There is only one minuscule issue with this breathtaking shtickel silver: the craftsman completely forgot to hollow out the inside. It is a solid block. The yungerman brings it home Friday afternoon, excitedly pours the aged yayin, and watches in horror as the grape juice splashes right off the flat top, completely ruining his freshly pressed white shirt. Next to this useless masterpiece sits a fifty-cent disposable plastic cup. The plastic cup is objectively worthless, devoid of any intrinsic material value or yichus. Yet, when the yungerman pours the yayin into the cheap cup, it miraculously holds the liquid perfectly. The solid silver piece, for all its external beauty, is practically an expensive paperweight, while the cheap, hollow cup actually functions as a true kli, ready to be used for Kiddush to bring kedushah into the home.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Next 169 0 R
>>
